# Venue rules for a body-tracked performer (RGBMoCap bridge). Only-Lang subset the Conductor parses today.
#
# A second check that does not trust the bridge: it runs inside the Conductor on whatever position
# arrives, from any sender. Bounds are a box (the language has no arithmetic, so no radius), looser
# than the bridge's 1.5 m circle at the corners. Edit the numbers for your stage.
#
# What a DENY does here: it signs a receipt into the governance log and the message returns an error.
# The position is ALREADY stored by then (the Conductor updates state, then evaluates rules), so this is
# a signed alarm, not a gate. Downstream consumers must not treat "accepted" as "in bounds" and must
# keep their own limits (hardware interlocks for lasers and moving heads).

harmony(1e-12)

if artist_tracking.position.x > 1.5 or artist_tracking.position.x < -1.5 or artist_tracking.position.y > 1.5 or artist_tracking.position.y < -1.5 then
    deny("Performer outside stage footprint")
end

if artist_tracking.position.z > 2.8 or artist_tracking.position.z < 0.0 then
    deny("Performer height outside 0 to 2.8 m")
end
